  partTitle: ZIGZAG CLASSIFIER
  partDescription: 'An upward current of inert gas held at exactly 0.015 m/s separates
    the solids by density: it fluidizes the light char dust (terminal velocity 0.0032
    m/s) and sweeps it out the side chute, but cannot lift the dense E-glass fibers
    (0.0368 m/s), which fall through zigzag baffles that scrub away residual char.'
